-- title:
--   Upper-triangular part of a hyperbolic twisted class: two cusp classes
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of fields whose Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma : L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$, in the sense that every $K$-automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in `Subgroup.zpowers σ`; write $\sigma$ also for the entrywise action `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.map (σ : L →+* L)` on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$. Let $t, t^w \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be such that $t$ is diagonal, $t = \mathrm{diag}(a,d)$ with $t_{10} = t_{01} = 0$, that $N_{L/K}(a/d) \neq 1$, and that $t^w$ is diagonal with $t^w_{00} = d$ and $t^w_{11} = a$. For $s \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ put $J(s) = \{\gamma : \exists b \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L),\ b_{10} = 0 \text{ and } s^{-1}(b^{-1}\gamma\,\sigma(b)) \in Z(\mathrm{GL}_2(L))\}$, i.e. $b^{-1}\gamma\,\sigma(b)$ is a central multiple of $s$ for some upper-triangular $b$. Then three assertions hold: first, the set of $\gamma$ with $\gamma_{10} = 0$ for which there exists $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ (unrestricted) with $t^{-1}(g^{-1}\gamma\,\sigma(g))$ central equals $J(t) \cup J(t^w)$; second, if moreover $N_{L/K}(a/d) \neq -1$ then $J(t)$ and $J(t^w)$ are disjoint; third, if $N_{L/K}(a/d) = -1$ then $J(t) = J(t^w)$.
--
--   This describes the upper-triangular members of a centre-saturated $\sigma$-twisted conjugacy class of hyperbolic norm type in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ as the union of the two Borel twisted classes attached to the two cusps $\mathrm{diag}(a,d)$ and $\mathrm{diag}(d,a)$ of the split torus, these being distinct except on the exceptional classes with $N_{L/K}(a/d) = -1$. It serves as the index bookkeeping for the constant term subtracted in the truncated hyperbolic contribution to the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2$, and is used in the computations of the corresponding truncated integrals over the Borel orbit.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LT_TwistedNorm_setOf_exists_mem_center_inter_setOf_apply_one_zero_eq_zero_eq_union_and_disjoint.lean

